# A family graph combines a property chain, inverse and functional properties.
# --owl-rl infers Alice's grandparent relation and two names for the same father,
# then reports that the stated difference between those names conflicts.
# This shows OWL 2 RL/RDF inference with a conflict retained in the Turtle output.
# Rules: W3C OWL 2 Profiles, https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs

@prefix : <https://example.org/family#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

# The ontology supplies the inverse, two-step chain and functional father property.
:parent owl:inverseOf :child ; rdfs:domain :Person ; rdfs:range :Person .
:grandparent owl:propertyChainAxiom (:parent :parent) .
:father a owl:FunctionalProperty ; rdfs:subPropertyOf :parent .

# Two parent steps make Alice a grandparent of both named fathers.
:Alice :parent :Bob .
:Bob :father :Charles, :Charlie .

# Functionality equates the two father names; this assertion makes that a conflict.
:Charles owl:differentFrom :Charlie .
